  "notes": "Only left-side photos (SU-GGI, SU-GGH, 2026) are on Commons; the right side is drawn the same and not checked. The side title's end is hidden by the engine and wing in every photo: its length (0.29) is read from the visible letters' pitch for eight letters, not seen. All three photos are from ahead and below: the fit is good to about 1–1.5 m along the body, the Horus feathers are seven tapered areas, each edge measured point by point on SU-GGI through the fit (crown feather from above the eye to a point ahead of door 2; five feathers sweeping back and down to the belly, alternating navy and blue; the cheek stroke), their navy-to-blue shading and the eye stay the logo's. The fin: four nested bands (blue, mid blue, light blue, then the white head) measured the same way, ringing the head over its top and down its forward side to the root; the navy feather lines in the head are the logo's. The right side has no Commons photo: drawn as the left's mirror (areas apply to both sides), not checked. The rest of the fleet (737, 777, 787, A320neo, A330) still wore the earlier scheme (white, blue Horus tail, 'EGYPTAIR' over the windows) in the photos seen; not drawn here.",
  "history": "New file (EgyptAir had no scheme here). This scheme came with the A350-900 deliveries (2025); EgyptAir's earlier scheme flies on the rest of the fleet (see notes)."
}